<wpt lat="51.515947" lon="5.440196"><name>DZC Wings of Liberation Museum, Best</name><desc>Tour day 1

Vehicles, aircraft, a Waco glider and the story of the Brabant liberation, on the edge of the ground the 101st landed on. The right start: it explains the plan before you drive the road.

Look at the map of the corridor first; the museum sits almost on Drop Zone B.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.512000" lon="5.491200"><name>DZC Son bridge &amp; 101st Airborne memorial</name><desc>Tour day 1

The Wilhelmina Canal crossing the Germans blew as the 506th arrived; the memorial stands on 17 Septemberplein beside the modern bridge. Engineers bridged the gap overnight; Easy crossed on the footbridge.

Stand at the water's edge: the far bank is where the 88 was.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.442500" lon="5.477500"><name>DZC Eindhoven — 18 Septemberplein</name><desc>Tour day 1

The square named for liberation day. Easy marched through cheering crowds here; that night the Luftwaffe bombed the city and the celebrations ended.

Walk the centre; the Philips town the paratroopers saw was largely rebuilt.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.564800" lon="5.459900"><name>DZC Sint-Oedenrode</name><desc>Tour day 1

The 502nd's town on the corridor; the highway through it is the original road. A good place to feel how narrow the whole operation was.

One road, two ditches, flat fields either side.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.586940" lon="5.492900"><name>DZC Koevering</name><desc>Tour day 1

The last cut of Hell's Highway, 24–25 September, on the straight road between Sint-Oedenrode and Veghel. Burnt-out convoys lined the road here while Arnhem fell.

Drive it slowly; the road is the exhibit.

Accuracy: MEDIUM — close to the spot.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.769250" lon="5.736650"><name>DZC Grave bridge (John S. Thompson bridge)</name><desc>Tour day 2

The Maas bridge taken intact by the 504th within minutes of landing on 17 September — the first Market Garden bridge secured.

The 82nd's textbook success, in contrast to Son.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.851100" lon="5.871700"><name>DZC Nijmegen — Waal crossing &amp; road bridge</name><desc>Tour day 2

On 20 September the 504th crossed the Waal in canvas boats under fire while the Guards' tanks rushed the road bridge. Half the boats were lost; the bridge fell at 19:00. The Waal crossing memorial stands on the south bank.

The width of the river is the story.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.785650" lon="5.937010"><name>DZC Freedom Museum, Groesbeek</name><desc>Tour day 2

The whole Market Garden and Rhineland story, on the 82nd's landing ground above Nijmegen.

Use the corridor map to place Easy's road inside the plan.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.961170" lon="5.813890"><name>DZC Driel — Polish brigade memorial</name><desc>Tour day 2

Where Sosabowski's Poles landed on 21 September and tried to reach the trapped British across the river. The Island begins here.

Look north across the Rhine to Oosterbeek.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.977500" lon="5.911500"><name>DZC John Frost Bridge, Arnhem</name><desc>Tour day 2

A bridge too far: Frost's 700 men held the north end for four days and were overrun on 21 September. The rebuilt bridge carries his name.

Stand at the north end; the houses the paras held were on this side.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.987750" lon="5.832670"><name>DZC Airborne Museum Hartenstein, Oosterbeek</name><desc>Tour day 2

Urquhart's headquarters hotel, now the museum of the Arnhem battle: nine days in the perimeter, then Operation Berlin's night evacuation.

The evacuation route ran south from here to the river — the same river Easy watched from the other side a month later.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.993600" lon="5.848420"><name>DZC Airborne War Cemetery, Oosterbeek</name><desc>Tour day 2

1,700 graves, mostly of the 1st Airborne Division. Local schoolchildren lay flowers here every September.

End the day here.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="50.008500" lon="5.738500"><name>DZC Bastogne War Museum &amp; Mardasson Memorial</name><desc>Tour day 3

The best single museum of the Bulge, beside the star-shaped American memorial. Do it first: it gives the siege its shape before you go into the woods.

Walk up to the Mardasson after the museum and look north-east — the Bois Jacques is the dark line on the skyline.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="50.019570" lon="5.764320"><name>DZC Bizory</name><desc>Tour day 3

The 506th's right-hand village; the road from here to Foy runs straight through the Easy Company positions.

Turn north onto the Foy road.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="50.028903" lon="5.756707"><name>DZC Easy Company memorial, Bois Jacques</name><desc>Tour day 3

Built by the Men of Easy Company Foundation on the Bizory–Foy road: fourteen names of Easy men killed here between 18 December and 13 January, and a text about −28 °C nights with little food and ammunition.

Read the names, then walk on into the wood.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="50.048420" lon="5.740870"><name>DZC Recogne German war cemetery</name><desc>Tour day 3

6,800 German dead from the Bulge, a kilometre from Foy — the men on the other side of the snowfield.

Place of remembrance.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

