<wpt lat="49.999255" lon="5.712212"><name>DZC 101st Airborne Museum — Le Mess</name><desc>Tour day 4

In the former officers' mess: uniforms, a bomb-shelter experience and a strong 101st collection. Avenue de la Gare 11.

Good for the human scale of the siege.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="50.010580" lon="5.716140"><name>DZC Bastogne Barracks</name><desc>Tour day 4

The Belgian barracks where General McAuliffe's staff worked in the cellars and where the German surrender demand was answered with 'Nuts!' on 22 December. Guided visits; large vehicle restoration hall.

The cellar is the real thing.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="50.000700" lon="5.717000"><name>DZC Place McAuliffe &amp; the Sherman</name><desc>Tour day 4

The square at the centre of the seven roads, with the general's bust and a Sherman tank knocked out at Renuamont.

Count the roads: this is why 101st was sent here.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/holland-bastogne.html

